      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "MI BOW (5) made it six minor placings from her past eight starts when she finished 9 metres away in second last time out over 2180m at Kilmore. That latest effort is good enough to take out a race like this. QUEEN TRUSCOTT (2) wasn't disgraced last time over 1710m at Ballarat, finishing 8 metres away from the winner in fourth. A nice draw on the front line should ensure a cosy run and rates a leading hope based on her best efforts. SPESHAL (7) found a couple better two runs back then things went sour last time when she broke and finished 10 metres back in fifth over 1690m at Maryborough. Tactics will be crucial from this wide draw. Meets a similar line up so if she behaves a big run is likely. LORD LOGAN (3) is a five-year-old entire from the Brent Lilley yard on debut. A nice draw on the front line should ensure a cosy run. Placed in a recent trial and any push in betting will add to the confidence.",
